// Standard ISO 9362
// A SWIFT/BIC number is a code that identifies a bank and its branch1. 
// It consists of 8 or 11 characters, made up of letters and numbers1. 
// The first 4 letters represent the bank name, the next 2 letters represent the country code, 
// the next 2 characters represent the location code, 
// and the last 3 characters (optional) represent the branch code1. 
// 
// For example, the SWIFT/BIC code for Scotiabank in Canada is NOSCCATTXXX

